# FreeBSD / OpenBSD / NetBSD only. UNTESTED -- no BSD has run cmdscribe.
#
# This is NOT for macOS. On macOS logger(1) posts to the unified log and
# never reaches syslogd's asl file routing, so nothing would ever be written
# to the file this rotates. Measured on macOS 27.2: an asl rule matching
# Facility local0 captured 41 unrelated lines and zero cmdscribe records.
# Use `install.sh --logfile` there instead.
#
# On the BSDs, base syslogd does honour facility routing, so this has a
# chance of being the right shape -- but "has a chance" is the same phrase
# the macOS version was written with, and it was wrong. Verify the file
# actually fills up before trusting it.
#
# Install alongside a syslog.conf rule routing local0 to the file:
#   install -m 0644 -o root -g wheel this /etc/newsyslog.d/cmdscribe.conf
#
# <logname>               <owner:group> <mode> <count> <size> <flags>
/var/log/cmdscribe.log    root:wheel    0600   12      10240 Z
